INSERT INTO sprintboarditems (ticket_id, title, domain, lane, stage, owner_role, status, blocker, next_step, approval_needed, notes)
VALUES (
  'MA-SEP-009',
  'Root-cause: direct_parent_lei/ultimate_parent_lei 0-of-43,578 populated (Known Issue 22.10)',
  'Entities',
  'data_identity',
  'ENG_DIAGNOSTIC',
  'Entities Product Lead',
  'ACTIVE',
  NULL,
  'Founder review of the proposed fix scope in notes below. No code touched, nothing deployed this session -- diagnostic only, per instruction. Once approved: fix entities-enrich.js runPhase3() (2 line-level changes) and entities-delta.js refreshParentExceptions() (1 line-level change, though that function is currently inert/unreachable so lower urgency), redeploy meridian-entities-enrich, then re-run Phase 3 against the existing backlog of already-processed entities (6,265 rows currently marked direct_parent_exception=NO_LINK_DECLARED need to be reset to NULL / re-queued so Phase 3''s WHERE clause picks them up again -- otherwise the fix only benefits entities not yet processed).',
  NULL,
  'ROOT CAUSE CONFIRMED: category (a), a genuine code bug -- NOT category (b), a GLEIF data-coverage reality. Two independent, compounding defects in entities-enrich.js runPhase3() (lines 227-330), both proven against the live GLEIF API this session: (1) line 253 reads `const relationships = detail.relationships ?? {}` -- GLEIF''s real lei-records/{lei} response has NO top-level relationships key; it lives at detail.data.relationships (confirmed live: fetched a real GLEIF record, top-level keys are only [meta, data], relationships is nested under data). This makes `relationships` always {} and relationships[direct-parent]/[ultimate-parent] always undefined, for every entity, unconditionally. (2) Even if (1) were fixed: for entities that DO have a real declared parent, GLEIF does not embed a data.id on the relationship object the way the code assumes (line 263: `const parentLei = relData.data.id`) -- it provides only a links object (e.g. links.lei-record) pointing to a separate resource that needs its own follow-up GET, confirmed live against Barclays Bank UK PLC (LEI 213800UUGANOMFJ9X769) and HSBC USA INC (LEI 549300LBOHZ4QSIWU288, entity_id 3331 -- this is OUR OWN entity_master row, not an external test case). relData.data is undefined in this real shape, so `if (!relData?.data) continue` (line 262) would also skip real parents even with fix (1) alone. Combined effect: directParentException is unconditionally computed as NO_LINK_DECLARED for every single entity Phase 3 has ever processed (since directParentRel is always undefined, hitting the `directParentRel === undefined ? NO_LINK_DECLARED : null` fallback at line 256-257) -- this exactly and completely explains both halves of the 0-of-43,578 finding: 0 real parents ever written, and all 6,265 already-processed entities uniformly stamped NO_LINK_DECLARED regardless of what GLEIF actually has on file. REAL-DATA PROOF OF IMPACT (not hypothetical): HSBC USA INC (our entity_id 3331) is marked direct_parent_exception=NO_LINK_DECLARED in production today, but GLEIF live-confirms its real direct parent is HSBC NORTH AMERICA HOLDINGS INC. (LEI 213800JCL1FHBQK3M654) -- a real, resolvable, currently-missed relationship. That parent entity does not yet exist in entity_master, so a fix run would exercise the existing (currently untested-in-production, since never reached) "create parent if missing" INSERT path at lines 270-289 -- flagged as its own small risk to verify carefully, not assumed correct just because it compiles. COVERAGE CAVEAT, stated honestly: a broader 30-entity random sample of already-processed operating entities (from Comstock Holding to Cannae Holdings, KKR Group Finance, major EU banks'' holding-company-level entities, etc.) showed zero real parent links in GLEIF for any of them -- consistent with GLEIF Level 2 (Reporting Relationship) data being genuinely voluntary and low-uptake in the largely-US 13F-derived population this project draws from. Both facts are true at once: the code is unconditionally broken (proven), AND the realistic post-fix population rate across the full 43,578 may be modest, not dramatic -- HSBC-style multinational subsidiaries are likely the sweet spot, not the median case. Do not oversell the fix''s expected yield. SILENT-FAILURE CHECK (Step 2): confirmed this is NOT a caught-and-hidden exception -- the catch blocks at lines 332-334 (Phase 3) and equivalent in entities-delta.js DO log via console.error, but the actual bug never throws (every step uses safe ?./?? operators), so the catch is never even reached. This is a "condition that''s silently always false," not a swallowed error. Also confirmed: entities-enrich.js writes no persisted run-summary to holdings_pipeline_state (unlike entities-delta.js''s delta_last_run/delta_entities_updated keys) -- no queryable historical invocation record exists beyond current entity_master state itself, a minor observability gap worth a mention but not the root cause. entities-delta.js: has the IDENTICAL bug (1) at line 220 of refreshParentExceptions(), but independently confirmed genuinely inert -- wrangler-entities-delta.toml has its cron trigger commented out (HOLD, gated on "ETF Phase 3"), and the /run HTTP fetch handler (lines 292-299) only invokes runDelta(), never refreshParentExceptions() -- that function is unreachable by any live path today. PROPOSED FIX SCOPE (not implemented, for Founder review): touched files entities-enrich.js (runPhase3, ~10 line change: read detail.data.relationships instead of detail.relationships; for a relationship with a links.lei-record URL but no embedded data.id, fetch that URL to resolve the real parent LEI before proceeding, mirroring the existing "fetch full parent detail" pattern already used one step later in the same function) and entities-delta.js (refreshParentExceptions, same 1-line top-level-path fix, lower urgency since currently unreachable -- fix for consistency/whenever Phase 5 unfreezes it, not urgent on its own). Safety/read-write impact: adds one extra GLEIF HTTP fetch per entity that has a real declared parent (to resolve the links-based relationship) -- bounded by the existing BATCH=45/invocation cap, well within the existing subrequest budget already used elsewhere in this Worker; no schema change; write shape unchanged (same UPDATE/INSERT statements, just reached correctly now). Separately needed: the 6,265 entities already incorrectly stamped NO_LINK_DECLARED will not be picked up by Phase 3''s own WHERE clause after the fix (direct_parent_exception IS NOT NULL excludes them) -- a one-time reset/requeue of that backlog is a second, explicit decision for the Founder, not silently bundled into "redeploy the fix."'
)
ON CONFLICT(ticket_id) DO UPDATE SET
  stage = excluded.stage,
  notes = excluded.notes,
  next_step = excluded.next_step,
  approval_needed = excluded.approval_needed,
  updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
